write_node_files() {
  cat > "$EVIDENCE/node-draft.txt" <<'EOF'
This is a Skyclause replay spike, not a live run. The trigger file is a labelled replay ("replay": true) of the real 2 November 2026 crossing, in Skyclause pilot/crossings-replay/sky.

First answer three platform questions, one line each:
TRIGGER: list every field the Google Drive trigger gave you (for example name, ID, MIME type, content), and say whether it included the file's content.
CONTENT: read the trigger file with the Google Drive connector. Say whether you could read its content; if you could, quote its crossing_id and replay values.
TIME: if the platform gives you the current date and time, give it and name where it came from. If it doesn't, write "TIME: none from the platform". Never estimate or guess the time.

Then draft one call for each entry in the file's "changes", numbered from 1:
- Subject: "Replay (2 Nov 2026): " followed by "{Mode}: {kind} {start}–{end}, {Ddd D Mmm} (Skyclause pilot)". Mode is the entry's "to" and kind is its window.kind, both with underscores as spaces and a capital first letter; start and end are window.start_myt and window.end_myt; the date is window.date.
- Body, plain text: "{Mode} for {kind} {start}–{end}, {Dddd D Mmmm YYYY}." Then "Why: {fired}. {input name} at {source_id} logged {value} {unit}, {state}, {age_min} min old at the crossing." Then "{blocked} off: MET keeps no warning history for 2 Nov 2026." Then these three lines exactly:
Skyclause is not a safety or emergency service. In an emergency, call 999.
Not affiliated with APU, KPT, JPS, MET, DOE, Prasarana/Rapid KL or the stadium.
Reply "unsubscribe" to stop these notices.

Use only values that appear in the file, and do no arithmetic: every number in a call must appear in the file.
End with a fenced JSON block: {"crossing_id": "...", "calls": [{"call": 1, "window_id": "...", "window": {...}, "subject": "...", "body": "..."}]}
EOF
  cat > "$EVIDENCE/request-info.txt" <<'EOF'
Message:
Review the replay calls the Draft step proposed. Reject or edit calls here; Approval comes next.

Question 1 (Short answer):
Calls to reject: their numbers, comma-separated, or none

Question 2 (Short answer):
Edits as "call number: new subject / new body", or none. Keep each subject's "Replay (2 Nov 2026):" start.
EOF
  cat > "$EVIDENCE/node-write.txt" <<EOF
This is a Skyclause replay spike. Write only to the four places below, and nowhere else: no other calendar, address, Jira label or spreadsheet.

Take the calls from the Draft step's JSON block and the Request info answers. Skip every call listed for rejection. Apply each edit to its call, keeping every subject's "Replay (2 Nov 2026):" start.

For each call that isn't rejected, in this order:
1. Jira Cloud, Create issue: project SKY, issue type Task, label replay. Summary: the call's subject. Description: the call's body. Keep the issue key.
2. Google Calendar, Create event on the calendar with ID $REPLAY_CALENDAR_ID only, never the primary calendar or any other: from window.date window.start_myt to window.date window.end_myt, time zone Asia/Kuala_Lumpur. Title: the call's subject. Description: the call's body, then "Jira {issue key}". No attendees. Keep the event link.
3. Gmail, Send message to $TEAM_ALERT_GMAIL and $TEAM_ALERT_OUTLOOK only, as plain text. Subject: the call's subject. Body: the call's body.
4. Google Drive, the spreadsheet with ID $SPIKE_SHEET_ID: read column A of its first tab with Get cell values, then with Update cell values write one row at the first empty row: crossing_id, call number, Jira issue key, calendar event link, "sent".

For each rejected call, only write a row to that spreadsheet: crossing_id, call number, "rejected".

Finish by listing every write you made, and every review you were asked for before it ran.
EOF
}

# ── Start ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
for tool in curl dig; do
  command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { warn "This wizard needs $tool; install it and re-run."; exit 1; }
done
if [[ -z "$GE_SETUP_DATE" ]]; then write_env GE_SETUP_DATE "$(myt +%F)"; fi
RECORD=$WORKFLOWS_DIR/setup-$GE_SETUP_DATE.md
EVIDENCE=$WORKFLOWS_DIR/setup-$GE_SETUP_DATE
mkdir -p "$EVIDENCE"
write_replay_file

banner "Gemini Enterprise setup for #49"

# ── Licence-free steps, in the ticket's order ──────────────────────────────
if open_stage "Pilot owner, domain and team inboxes" TEAM_ALERT_EMAILS; then
  say "Who's needed:"
  step "Pilot owner: this whole run, about 2½ hours of console work."
  step "Domain admin: the SPF, DKIM and DMARC records (about 15 minutes, plus propagation)."
  step "A teammate: edits, rejects and approves the spike runs (about 10 minutes)."
  note "By 12:00 MYT on Saturday 7 November the app and its Drive, Gmail, Calendar and Jira actions must work, or comment on #47. It's $(now_myt) now."
  printf '\n'
  say "The pilot owner is one Google Workspace account in the GE-licensed domain (#7)."
  say "Consumer @gmail.com accounts can't use the Drive, Gmail and Calendar connectors."
  while :; do
    ask_match WORKSPACE_DOMAIN "Workspace domain the pilot owner signs in with (no @):" \
      '^[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?(\.[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?)+$' "a lower-case domain name"
    case $WORKSPACE_DOMAIN in
      gmail.com | googlemail.com) warn "That's a consumer domain; the connectors need a Workspace domain." ;;
      *) break ;;
    esac
  done
  if [[ "$WORKSPACE_DOMAIN" == m1ku.tech || "$WORKSPACE_DOMAIN" == *.m1ku.tech ]]; then
    warn "m1ku.tech DNS is changed only through the Cloudflare API, only under skyclause.m1ku.tech, and never at the m1ku.tech apex (MX, SPF, DMARC). Check with the zone owner before adding records."
  fi
  ask_match PILOT_OWNER_EMAIL "Pilot owner's address:" "^[^@[:space:]]+@${WORKSPACE_DOMAIN//./\\.}$" "an address @$WORKSPACE_DOMAIN"
  say "Replay notices go only to TEAM_ALERT_EMAILS: one Gmail address and one Outlook address."
  ask_match TEAM_ALERT_GMAIL "Teammate's Gmail address:" "$EMAIL_RE" "an email address"
  ask_match TEAM_ALERT_OUTLOOK "Teammate's Outlook address:" "$EMAIL_RE" "an email address"
  write_env TEAM_ALERT_EMAILS "$TEAM_ALERT_GMAIL,$TEAM_ALERT_OUTLOOK"
  end_stage
fi

if open_stage "Jira: Free site and project SKY" JIRA_PROJECT; then
  open_url "https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/free"
  step "Sign up for Jira Cloud Free and pick a site name; the site is https://<name>.atlassian.net."
  step "Create a project with key SKY whose issue types include Task. (Jira may call issues work items.)"
  while :; do
    ask JIRA_SITE "Site URL (https://<name>.atlassian.net):"
    JIRA_SITE=${JIRA_SITE%/}
    if [[ "$JIRA_SITE" != https://* ]]; then JIRA_SITE=https://$JIRA_SITE; fi
    if [[ "$JIRA_SITE" =~ ^https://[A-Za-z0-9-]+\.atlassian\.net$ ]]; then break; fi
    warn "That doesn't look right: https://<name>.atlassian.net."
  done
  write_env JIRA_SITE "$JIRA_SITE"
  say "Fetching the instance ID from $JIRA_SITE/_edge/tenant_info:"
  if tenant=$(curl -sS "$JIRA_SITE/_edge/tenant_info" 2>&1); then
    JIRA_CLOUD_ID=$(printf '%s' "$tenant" | sed -n 's/.*"cloudId":"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p')
  else
    JIRA_CLOUD_ID=""
  fi
  if [[ -n "$JIRA_CLOUD_ID" ]]; then
    write_env JIRA_CLOUD_ID "$JIRA_CLOUD_ID"
  else
    warn "No cloudId came back: ${tenant:0:200}"
    step "Open $JIRA_SITE/_edge/tenant_info and copy cloudId."
    ask_match JIRA_CLOUD_ID "cloudId:" '^[0-9a-f-]{36}$' "a UUID"
  fi
  until confirm "Is project SKY there, with issue type Task?"; do pause "Create it, then press Enter."; done
  write_env JIRA_PROJECT "confirmed $(now_myt)"
  end_stage
fi

if open_stage "Jira: OAuth app" JIRA_OAUTH_APP_NAME; then
  say "Create the OAuth 2.0 app the Google connector signs in with."
  open_url "https://developer.atlassian.com/console/myapps/"
  step "Create → OAuth 2.0 Integration → a name → agree to Atlassian's developer terms → Create."
  step "Authorization → OAuth 2.0 (3LO) → Add → Callback URL: $CALLBACK → Save changes."
  step "Permissions → Jira API → Add → Configure → Classic scopes → Edit scopes:"
  step "  read:jira-user, read:jira-work, write:jira-work, manage:jira-project → Save."
  step "Distribution → Edit → Distribution status: Sharing. Vendor: Google. Privacy policy: https://policies.google.com."
  step "  Does your app store personal data?: Yes, tick the personal data reporting API confirmation → Save changes."
  step "Settings shows the Client ID and Client secret. Leave the tab open: you paste them straight into the Google console in the Jira data store stage. This wizard never asks for them."
  ask_match JIRA_OAUTH_APP_NAME "App name:" '.+'
  end_stage
fi

if open_stage "Jira: admin consent and user management" JIRA_ADMIN_GROUP; then
  say "As an Atlassian organisation admin:"
